{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumObservableUniverses.CategoricalActionUnique","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumObservableUniverses.CategoricalActionUnique","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Rigid.Basic"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalAction.unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalAction.unique","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-action-unique.lean#L43-L55","doc":"**Uniqueness of the categorical action (given Φ).**\n\nAny two morphisms `S₁, S₂ : 𝟙 ⟶ 𝟙` that both factor as the categorical\naction composite for the same `(Φ, swap)` are equal — both equal the\ncategorical trace `tr(Φ) = categoricalAction Φ swap`. This faithfully\nencodes the manuscript's claim that `𝒮_Φ` is uniquely determined. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:categorical-action-unique","label":"prop:categorical-action-unique","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-action-unique.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.categoricalAction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.categoricalAction","kind":"def","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-action-unique.lean#L36-L41","doc":"**Categorical action** `𝒮_Φ : 𝟙 ⟶ 𝟙` of `Φ : A ⟶ A` — the composite\n`η_ ≫ (Φ ▷ Aᘁ) ≫ swap ≫ ε_` (definitionally the trace `tr(Φ)`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}